          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Historical Background</strong><br>\nThroughout history, women in Israel and Palestine have often had different roles and rights. In traditional societies, they often had fewer rights than men. However, the role of women began to change over time, especially with the formation of the State of Israel in 1948, where women received equal rights as men.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legal Rights in Israel</strong><br>\nIn Israel, women have equal rights as men through laws and regulations. They can vote and be elected, and there are laws against discrimination of women. Women in Israel also have the right to equal pay for equal work, although pay gaps still exist.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Social Roles in Israel</strong><br>\nIn Israeli society, women have access to education and can pursue careers in many fields. There are also women in high political offices. However, there are also traditional or religious communities where the roles of men and women are strictly separated.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
