          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Political Participation in Palestine</strong><br>\nPolitical participation of women in Palestine is lower compared to Israel, but there are women who are active in political parties and organizations. There are also efforts by women's rights groups to promote women's political participation and gender equality.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Education and Career in Palestine</strong><br>\nEducation for women in Palestine is often limited, and there are fewer career opportunities for women compared to men. However, there are also women who are successful in the fields of education, medicine, and other professions, and there are efforts to improve access to education and career opportunities.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Comparison between Israel and Palestine</strong><br>\nThe situation of women in Israel and Palestine shows clear differences due to the various political, social, and cultural contexts. While women in Israel have more rights and opportunities, there are many challenges in Palestine. However, both areas also have commonalities, such as the important role of women in the family and community.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
